{"folder":null,"name":"Cranial Trauma System","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/b/b6/ME3_Pistol_Cranial_Trauma_Systeme.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A targeting VI and barrel assembly optimized for precision shots against the head and upper cervical spine. The system calculates the minimum kinetic energy required to defeat helmet plating at specific trajectories and adjusts round velocity accordingly, ensuring penetration without sacrificing accuracy at range. Designed for pistols. When you hit a target with a pistol against their flat-footed or off-guard AC, deal an additional 1d6 precision damage.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a pistol.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"cranial-trauma-system","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"rare"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"cranial-trauma-system","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"a6f9b597dbb87232"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Extended Barrel I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/c/cb/ME3_SMG_High_Caliber_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A longer barrel with an extended kinetic acceleration chamber that increases the muzzle velocity of outgoing rounds. The additional distance allows the mass effect coils more time to impart momentum, resulting in harder-hitting impacts across all fire modes. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Grants a +1 item bonus to weapon damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"extended-barrel-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"extended-barrel","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"d02dae522aa372e4"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Extended Barrel II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/c/cb/ME3_SMG_High_Caliber_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A military-specification extended barrel with a reinforced acceleration chamber and precision-tuned coil spacing. Rounds exit with significantly greater force than a standard barrel configuration allows, and the added length improves accuracy over the weapon's effective range as a secondary benefit. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Grants a +2 item bonus to weapon damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"extended-barrel-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"extended-barrel","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"c45061353017985e"}
{"folder":null,"name":"High-Velocity Barrel I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/83/ME3_Assault_Rifle_High-Velocity_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A specially rifled barrel with hardened interior lining that increases round velocity to levels sufficient to punch through light armor plating. Rounds traveling at these velocities carry enough kinetic force that conventional armor weaves cannot fully absorb the impact. Your weapon's attacks ignore 5 points of physical resistance.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"high-velocity-barrel-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"high-velocity-barrel","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"5405967959f648b3"}
{"folder":null,"name":"High-Velocity Barrel II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/83/ME3_Assault_Rifle_High-Velocity_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An advanced high-velocity barrel with a tungsten-lined bore and enhanced mass effect coil configuration. Rounds exit at velocities that defeat medium armor plating and penetrate kinetic barrier fields before the field can fully dampen the impact. Originally developed for anti-Geth operations where standard round velocities proved insufficient. Your weapon's attacks ignore 10 points of physical resistance.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"high-velocity-barrel-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"high-velocity-barrel","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"e0744c281652c54c"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Magazine Upgrade I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/5/51/ME3_SMG_Heat_Sink.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An extended heat sink and thermal clip assembly that increases the number of rounds a weapon can fire before requiring a heat sink swap. The larger thermal mass absorbs more heat per cycle, allowing the weapon to sustain fire well past the point a standard configuration would demand a reload. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Increases the weapon's ammo capacity by 50% (round up).</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"magazine-upgrade-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"magazine-upgrade","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"e9780e654435e5c8"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Magazine Upgrade II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/5/51/ME3_SMG_Heat_Sink.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A double-capacity heat sink assembly using high-density composite thermal materials that absorb nearly twice the heat of a standard clip before requiring replacement. Soldiers equipped with this modification can sustain fire through engagements that would exhaust standard-capacity weapons multiple times over. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Doubles the weapon's ammo capacity.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"magazine-upgrade-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"magazine-upgrade","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"681314ae298d495d"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Melee Stunner I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/9/95/ME3_Shotgun_Blade_Attachment.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A compact electroshock emitter fitted to the weapon's frame near the barrel that discharges on contact during a pistol-whip or frame strike. The charge is calibrated to disrupt nervous system function without lethal effect, creating a brief window of incapacitation that operatives can exploit. Designed for pistols. When you Strike with a pistol as a melee weapon and hit, the target is flat-footed until the start of your next turn.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a pistol.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"melee-stunner-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"melee-stunner","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"f7e4bb7167f22462"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Melee Stunner II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/9/95/ME3_Shotgun_Blade_Attachment.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A high-voltage frame-mounted stun emitter that delivers a full nervous system override on contact, briefly overwhelming the target's ability to take voluntary action. The system includes a charge capacitor that can sustain multiple discharges per engagement without drawing from the weapon's heat sink. Developed by Alliance Intelligence for close-quarters capture operations. Designed for pistols. When you Strike with a pistol as a melee weapon and hit, the target is stunned 1.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a pistol.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"melee-stunner-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"melee-stunner","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"9846e1d6cfc0d7b0"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Omni-Blade","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/6/6a/ME3_Assault_Rifle_Omni-Blade.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A micro-fabricated crystalline blade generated from the weapon's omni-tool interface and bonded to the barrel or foregrip. Unlike standalone omni-blades, the weapon-mounted version is structurally reinforced against the recoil forces of sustained fire and can be deployed without removing the hand from the grip. The blade glows orange with thermal energy from the weapon's heat dissipation system. Your weapon gains the versatile (slashing) trait and deals 1d6 slashing damage on melee Strikes.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"omni-blade","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"omni-blade","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":250}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"40804d98f33cc78b"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Power Magnifier I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/b/bc/ME3_Pistol_Heavy_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A reinforced barrel and enhanced coil assembly designed specifically for pistol frames, increasing kinetic output without requiring the larger receiver of a rifle-class weapon. The upgrade effectively turns a standard combat pistol into a weapon capable of punching through armor grades it was not rated for. Designed for pistols. Grants a +1 item bonus to weapon damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a pistol.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"power-magnifier-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"power-magnifier","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"53587a95e1c25abd"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Power Magnifier II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/b/bc/ME3_Pistol_Heavy_Barrel.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A high-output barrel assembly with a heavy-duty kinetic coil stack that maximizes the velocity of each round fired from a pistol platform. The upgrade draws additional power from the weapon's thermal cell to sustain the enhanced field output, but the result is a pistol that hits with the force of a weapon two classes above it. Preferred by infiltrators and agents who need stopping power without the bulk of a rifle. Designed for pistols. Grants a +2 item bonus to weapon damage rolls.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a pistol.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"power-magnifier-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"power-magnifier","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"c92f7ada0e71f27f"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Scope I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/7/71/ME3_SMG_Scope_Upgrade.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A low-magnification targeting scope with an integrated rangefinder and windage compensation system. Allows the user to reliably engage targets at distances beyond the weapon's standard effective range. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Increases the weapon's range increment by 20 feet.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"scope-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"scope","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"20fe66d09904df13"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Scope II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/7/71/ME3_SMG_Scope_Upgrade.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A high-magnification combat scope with an advanced rangefinder VI, atmospheric correction algorithms, and integrated target tracking. Designed for engagements at distances where standard iron sights become unreliable. Widely used by scout and infiltrator units who operate ahead of the main line. Compatible with any ranged weapon. Increases the weapon's range increment by 40 feet.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"scope-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"scope","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"cf4b05729ab61142"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Shredder Mod I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/4/42/ME3_Shotgun_Shredder_Module.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A modified shot dispersal pattern that introduces irregular, tumbling pellets into the spread. The irregular projectiles tear rather than punch through tissue, leaving wounds that resist natural clotting. Particularly effective against organic targets that lack full-body armor coverage. Designed for shotguns. On a hit, the target takes 1d4 persistent bleed damage.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a shotgun.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"shredder-mod-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"shredder-mod","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"ee7d063e95841f85"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Shredder Mod II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/4/42/ME3_Shotgun_Shredder_Module.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An advanced shredder configuration using serrated flechette sub-projectiles that deploy on impact and embed in tissue before the main pellet mass follows through. The flechettes tear open wounds that are difficult to seal even with medi-gel, and the sheer volume of penetrating fragments makes clean wounds nearly impossible. Originally developed by mercenary groups for anti-personnel operations in close quarters. Designed for shotguns. On a hit, the target takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a shotgun.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"shredder-mod-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"shredder-mod","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"6364503a9449c63e"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Smart Choke I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/e/ee/ME3_Shotgun_Smart_Choke.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An adjustable choke collar that narrows the shot spread at the muzzle, tightening pellet groupings at range. The choke's internal geometry is tuned to maintain lethality at the tighter spread angle rather than just redirecting the pellets. Useful when a shotgun needs to reach targets beyond its standard effective envelope. Designed for shotguns. Increases the weapon's range increment by 10 feet.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a shotgun.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"smart-choke-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"smart-choke","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"6951413d84677765"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Smart Choke II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/e/ee/ME3_Shotgun_Smart_Choke.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A precision variable-choke system controlled by a targeting VI that dynamically adjusts spread angle based on target range data fed from the weapon's sensors. At close range it widens for maximum coverage; at distance it tightens to near-rifle precision. The result is a shotgun that can perform effectively at ranges previously requiring a dedicated rifle. Designed for shotguns. Increases the weapon's range increment by 20 feet.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a shotgun.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"smart-choke-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"smart-choke","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"f19db8f01de7cb10"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Stability Damper I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/87/ME3_SMG_Ultralight_Materials.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A recoil-absorbing stock and foregrip assembly that counteracts the muzzle climb and barrel drift caused by sustained automatic fire. The damper allows the shooter to maintain a tighter grouping during full-auto bursts without physical strength compensating for weapon movement. Designed for use with rifles and submachine guns. Grants a +1 item bonus to attack rolls made with automatic fire.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a weapon with the automatic trait.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"stability-damper-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"stability-damper","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"9cbcda64390dba6e"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Stability Damper II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/87/ME3_SMG_Ultralight_Materials.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An advanced gyroscopic stabilization system integrated into the weapon's frame that actively counteracts recoil forces during automatic fire. The internal gyros detect barrel deviation in real time and correct before the next round fires, keeping the weapon on-target regardless of fire rate. Originally developed for Cerberus heavy infantry operating automatic weapons at extreme sustained rates. Grants a +2 item bonus to attack rolls made with automatic fire.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a weapon with the automatic trait.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"stability-damper-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":7},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"stability-damper","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":700}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"ef1f4429858c1055"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Thermal Scope I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/6/6c/ME3_Sniper_Rifle_Thermal_Scope.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A thermal imaging scope that overlays heat signatures onto the targeting display, allowing the sniper to identify biological targets behind light cover and track movement through smoke or debris. The heat signature mapping highlights organ-dense areas and joint gaps in armor, guiding rounds toward targets' most vulnerable points. Designed for sniper rifles. On a successful aimed shot, deal an additional 1d6 precision damage.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a sniper rifle.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"thermal-scope-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"thermal-scope","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":250}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"663a36671d35ae0d"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Thermal Scope II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/6/6c/ME3_Sniper_Rifle_Thermal_Scope.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>An advanced multi-spectrum thermal scope combining infrared imaging with a predictive targeting VI that calculates optimal impact points in real time. The system cross-references enemy species anatomy databases to identify the most lethal aiming solutions, accounting for environmental interference and barrier field distortion. Used exclusively by N7 infiltrators and Shadow Broker wetwork specialists. Designed for sniper rifles. On a successful aimed shot, deal an additional 2d6 precision damage.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure. Requires a sniper rifle.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"thermal-scope-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"rare"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":9},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"thermal-scope","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":2000}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"1b869a32ff04a3f1"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Ultralight Materials I","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/87/ME3_SMG_Ultralight_Materials.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A partial frame replacement using carbon-ceramic composite materials that retain the weapon's structural integrity while substantially reducing its mass. The lighter weapon is easier to move with, transitions between targets faster, and contributes less fatigue to extended carry. Favored by operatives who spend long missions on foot. Reduces the weapon's Bulk by 1 (minimum 0).</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"ultralight-materials-1","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"common"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":3},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"ultralight-materials","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":100}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"5d5122d4bb0051aa"}
{"folder":null,"name":"Ultralight Materials II","type":"equipment","effects":[],"img":"https://static.wikia.nocookie.net/masseffect/images/8/87/ME3_SMG_Ultralight_Materials.png","flags":{},"ownership":{"default":0},"_stats":{"compendiumSource":null,"duplicateSource":null,"exportSource":null,"coreVersion":"13.351","systemId":"pf2e","systemVersion":"7.12.2","lastModifiedBy":null},"system":{"description":{"gm":"","value":"<p>A full-frame reconstruction using aerospace-grade ultralight alloys and hollow-core carbon fiber components. The weapon retains full combat reliability at a fraction of its original mass, to the point where carrying it feels negligible even during extended operations. Developed originally for Salarian STG agents who carry multiple weapons simultaneously. Reduces the weapon's Bulk by 1 (minimum 0) and grants +5 feet to your Speed while this weapon is your primary drawn weapon.</p><p><strong>Activate</strong> — Install on weapon during a 10-minute field maintenance procedure.</p>"},"rules":[],"slug":"ultralight-materials-2","_migration":{"version":0.955,"lastMigration":null,"previous":null},"traits":{"otherTags":[],"value":["tech"],"rarity":"uncommon"},"publication":{"title":"Mass Effect Homebrew","authors":"","license":"ORC","remaster":true},"level":{"value":5},"quantity":1,"baseItem":"ultralight-materials","bulk":{"value":0},"price":{"value":{"gp":250}},"equipped":{"carryType":"worn","invested":null},"usage":{"value":"installed-in-a-weapon"},"identification":{"status":"identified","unidentified":{"name":"Unknown Mod","img":"systems/pf2e/icons/unidentified_item_icons/worn-item.webp","data":{"description":{"value":""}}},"misidentified":{}},"subitems":[],"specific":null},"_id":"862d10bc31ec31de"}
